WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.409
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:06.780
SPEAKER: Identity and
Access Management, or IAM,

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.330
in Google Cloud gives
you fine-grained control

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.500
over permissions.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.840
But it can be complex to manage.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.940
The IAM Policy
Troubleshooter tool

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.010
can help in investigating
issues as to why

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.520
a user has access to a resource
or doesn't have permission

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.170
to call an API.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.540
Let's walk through how to use
the Policy Troubleshooter.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.100
We can access Policy
Troubleshooter

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.650
using the Cloud Console,
the G Cloud command line

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.960
tool, or the REST API.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.180
For simple queries,
using the Cloud Console

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.430
is easy and includes
a visual aid.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.160
For more complex scenarios,
consider using the G Cloud

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.230
tool or the REST API.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.990
In this video, we'll focus on
using Policy Troubleshooter

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.060
through the Cloud
Console and getting

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.130
the details of a project.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.990
First off, we'll
need three parameters

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.200
to use Policy Troubleshooter--
principal, resource,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.490
and permission.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.290
The Principal field
is the email address

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:59.010
to check, which can refer to
a user or a service account.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.600
Let's use a user account with
the email user@tse.joonix.net.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.519
The Resource field
is the full name

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:07.590
of the resource we
want to test against.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:11.070
The path of the full name varies
depending on the resource type.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.320
For example, the
path for our project

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.840
is cloudresourceman
ager.googleapis.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.025
com/projects/myproject.

00:01:20.042 --> 00:01:21.750
You can see a full
list of resource names

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.837
in the documentation, or you can
use the autocomplete function.

00:01:25.837 --> 00:01:27.420
The Permission field
is the permission

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.190
we're checking the user for.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.620
Similar to the Resource
field, a list of permissions

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.110
will be presented
as we start to type.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:37.230
Let's use
resourcemanager.projects.git,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.870
which grants access to
retrieve the project.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.460
For a complete list,
of permissions.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.400
Check the permissions
reference documentation.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.680
The required permission
to access a resource

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.613
may also be displayed as part
of a Permission Denied error.

00:01:48.613 --> 00:01:51.030
You can always refer to the
specific product documentation

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.250
page for a list of
roles and permissions

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.290
that are required to
access the resources.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.600
We can also add additional
resources and permissions

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:01.330
to check for the principal
by clicking on Add Additional

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.100
Pair, if desired.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.500
We'll click on Check API
Call, and our results page

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.222
will come up.

00:02:06.222 --> 00:02:07.930
By default, the results
will be displayed

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:09.729
in compact view,
which will only show

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.729
the roles that contain
the permission that we've

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:12.460
checked for.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.650
We can click the toggle
to see the full view,

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.550
displaying all the roles for
our resource's IAM policy.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.170
At the top of the
page, we can quickly

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.560
see whether the user is granted
the permission on the resource.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.390
We can see that our
user has the permission

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.720
for resourcemanager.projects.git
in our project.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.580
Additional details
on the policy results

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.110
are also displayed below.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.240
The first warning, "You
do not have permission

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.280
to view all policy
bindings," may

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.400
occur if this is a resource
that's under an organization.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.900
The user doesn't
have the permission

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.380
to view hierarchical IAM
policies on the organization

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.270
and/or the folder.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.950
To resolve, this
the user would need

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.170
a role, such as
Security Reviewer,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.602
at the organization level.

00:02:51.602 --> 00:02:53.560
The second warning, "You
do not have permission

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.500
to view specific
group memberships,"

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.020
may be due to the user not
having group admin permissions.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.150
To resolve this, a G
Suite administrator

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.600
could grant the user a role
with the groups.read permission.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.430
The left pane contains
a list of roles

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:09.460
that apply to the given
resource and an icon, which

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:12.130
shows if our user has
a binding to that role.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.620
We can click on the role
to highlight the specifics.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.360
The green check next
to the owner role

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:19.990
indicates that this binding
grants access to our user.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.810
The right pane displays the
raw text of each binding,

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.420
highlighting each line
for the roles and members.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.000
Lines that don't match
our user are shown in red,

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.928
and ones that match are green.

00:03:29.928 --> 00:03:31.720
Yellow means that the
policy troubleshooter

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.580
can't evaluate the binding.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.500
In this case, it's
likely due to the warning

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.210
earlier about the
lack of permissions

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.742
to view group memberships.

00:03:38.742 --> 00:03:40.450
Read more about the
Policy Troubleshooter

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.325
in the documentation.

00:03:41.325 --> 00:03:44.010
[MUSIC PLAYING]

